WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.235
-Today might have been
the most devastating day

00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:04.837
of the Trump presidency so far.

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:07.607
A key witness to the Ukraine
scheme provided evidence

00:00:07.607 --> 00:00:09.142
that there was a quid pro quo

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.511
and that it was ordered by
the President himself.

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:14.047
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:18.284
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.686
Today we heard from Trump's
hand-picked ambassador

00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:23.089
to the European Union,
a guy named Gordon Sondland.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.225
Sondland's testimony was
explosive, shocking,

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:27.427
and jaw-dropping,
and if you don't believe me,

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:30.096
let's just fast-forward to
the moment when after Democrats

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:31.430
finish questioning Sondland,

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:34.600
the camera cut over to
GOP Congressman Devin Nunes.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.469
-That concludes our 45 minutes.

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:39.005
I now recognize Mr. Nunes.

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:40.873
-Oh.
-Okay.

00:00:40.873 --> 00:00:42.709
Why don't we take
a 5- or 10-minute break?

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:43.443
-Thank you.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:45.011
-Man, look at his face.

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:46.379
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:50.283
He looks like he just walked in
on his parents having sex

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:52.752
with someone else's parents.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.153
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:56.022
There's only two explanations
to that face.

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:57.723
Either he just heard
lengthy testimony

00:00:57.723 --> 00:01:00.159
detailing a criminal scheme
so shocking it could bring down

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:01.461
the presidency of Donald Trump,

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:04.063
or he sharted
and he's trying to remember

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:06.266
how far away
his backup pants are.

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:07.700
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.136
Sondland's testimony didn't just
go straight to President Trump

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:13.038
but also involved virtually
everybody at the highest levels

00:01:13.038 --> 00:01:14.206
of the administration.

00:01:14.206 --> 00:01:16.776
Sondland named every name
in the book.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:19.912
-Secretary Perry,
Ambassador Volker,

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:23.749
Rudy Giuliani, Secretary Pompeo,
Brian McCormack,

00:01:23.749 --> 00:01:26.252
Ms. Kenna,
Chief of Staff Mulvaney,

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:29.488
Rob Blair, Vice President Pence,
A$AP Rocky.

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:34.427
-He named A$AP Rocky!
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:36.996
Sondland name-checked virtually
all of Trump's senior aides,

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:39.599
Vice President Mike Pence,
Secretary of State Mike Pompeo,

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:42.201
Energy Secretary Rick Perry,
Chief of Staff Mick Mulvaney,

00:01:42.201 --> 00:01:44.137
and Trump's lawyer,
Rudy Giuliani.

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:47.507
Even the White House janitor was
like, "Am I gonna go to jail?"

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:48.508
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:50.209
In short,
today we learned yet again

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:51.811
that the entire Trump
White House

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.447
is basically
one giant criminal conspiracy.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:57.483
This was like the "Wizard of Oz"
of impeachment testimony.

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:59.151
"You were there,
and you were there,

00:01:59.151 --> 00:02:00.753
and you were there too, mate!

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:02.255
You were the scarecrow!"

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:03.756
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:06.926
Now, before we get to the rest
of today's bombshell testimony,

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:09.262
it's important to provide
some context for why today

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:11.331
was the most shocking day
of testimony so far.

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:13.065
Throughout this
impeachment process,

00:02:13.065 --> 00:02:15.034
we've been watching
the Republican argument

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:16.636
morph in real time,

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.937
which makes sense because Trump
always looks like he's morphing.

00:02:18.937 --> 00:02:20.473
He looks like an animorph

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:22.742
who's halfway between
human and bobcat.

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.443
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.443 --> 00:02:26.912
For example, you'll recall
that Trump began by insisting

00:02:26.912 --> 00:02:29.415
there was no quid pro quo
with Ukraine

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.317
and that his phone call
with the president of Ukraine,

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:33.019
in which Trump
literally said the words,

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:35.021
"I would like you to do us
a favor" was perfect.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.822
But as the impeachment process
has proved,

00:02:36.822 --> 00:02:38.057
it definitely was not perfect.

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:39.792
Republicans have changed
their argument.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.728
For example, yesterday
two credible witnesses

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:43.996
who were on Trump's call
called it

00:02:43.996 --> 00:02:45.765
unusual,
inappropriate, and improper.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:47.300
And even a Republican witness,

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.802
a national security official
named Tim Morrison,

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:52.104
said straight up that Sondland
had told him

00:02:52.104 --> 00:02:54.907
Trump was holding up the
aid to Ukraine in exchange for

00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:57.209
a promise from Ukraine
to announce publicly

00:02:57.209 --> 00:02:59.445
that they were investigating
Trump's political rivals.

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:02.782
-What did Ambassador Sondland
say to tell you

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:05.618
that he told Mr. Yermak?

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:12.157
-That the Ukrainians would have
to have the prosecutor general

00:03:12.157 --> 00:03:15.228
make a statement with respect to
the investigations

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:17.163
as a condition
of having the aid lifted.

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:19.399
-There you go.
That's literally a quid pro quo.

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:22.034
Republicans actually thought
calling this guy as a witness

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:23.435
would be a good idea.

00:03:23.435 --> 00:03:25.437
They thought he would help their
case, but he only made it worse.

00:03:25.437 --> 00:03:27.206
It's like if you murdered a guy

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:29.242
and called his ghost
as your witness.

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:30.076
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:31.510
"He's the one who killed me!"

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:32.478
"Damn it, ghost!"

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:33.612
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.612 --> 00:03:36.148
"I thought you were on my side!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.148 --> 00:03:37.616
So, after Tuesday's hearings,

00:03:37.616 --> 00:03:40.219
Republicans decided to change
their argument again.

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:43.222
A house GOP aide described the
change of messaging this way.

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:45.491
It has gone from
"there is no quid pro quo"

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.693
"to there's a quid and quo
but not a pro,"

00:03:47.693 --> 00:03:50.429
to "even if there was a quid pro
quo, it's not that bad.

00:03:50.429 --> 00:03:52.231
This is just
how things are done.

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:54.633
You can say it's bad,
but it's not impeachable."

00:03:54.633 --> 00:03:57.769
My God, look how much
their argument has changed.

00:03:57.769 --> 00:03:59.872
This would be like if you got
pulled over and said,

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:01.540
"I wasn't speeding.
Okay, I was speeding.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.109
Everyone speeds.
I was late for my job.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:04.877
I work at the hospital.
So does my wife.

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:06.845
And she's having a baby,
and I was barely speeding.

00:04:06.845 --> 00:04:08.881
Fine, I was really speeding
and my wife's not pregnant,

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:09.915
and I don't have a wife.

00:04:09.915 --> 00:04:12.251
And also I'm drunk --
on cocaine."

00:04:12.251 --> 00:04:14.787
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:16.555
Which brings us
to today's hearing.

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:18.491
Remember Sondland,
hand-picked by Trump.

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:20.760
He's a businessman who donated
a million dollars

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.161
to Trump's inaugural committee

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:24.463
and he was a central figure
in Ukraine policy.

00:04:24.463 --> 00:04:25.932
In fact, according to Morrison,

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:27.633
officials in
the Trump administration

00:04:27.633 --> 00:04:30.102
even coined a term
for Gordon Sondland's role

00:04:30.102 --> 00:04:31.270
in Ukraine policy.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:33.272
-Among the discussions
I had with Dr. Hill

00:04:33.272 --> 00:04:36.976
were about Ambassador Sondland.

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:39.411
I think she might have coined it
"the Gordon problem."

00:04:39.411 --> 00:04:41.814
-That's what they called it,
"the Gordon problem?"

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:44.583
That sounds like a indie movie
about a single guy in his 40s

00:04:44.583 --> 00:04:45.685
starring Ben Stiller.

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:47.519
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.519 --> 00:04:49.722
So today Sondland
had the chance to respond.

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:52.692
Again, Sondland, a key middleman
between Trump and Ukraine,

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:54.526
and he wrote down
what was happening

00:04:54.526 --> 00:04:56.295
in several infamous
text messages,

00:04:56.295 --> 00:04:58.431
and he started out his testimony
by stating

00:04:58.431 --> 00:05:00.900
clearly and unequivocally
that everything they did,

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.369
they did at the direction
of the President himself.

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:08.140
-Secretary Perry,
Ambassador Volker, and I

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:12.779
worked with Mr. Rudy Giuliani
on Ukraine matters

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:16.949
at the express direction of the
President of the United States.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:19.285
We followed
the President's orders.

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:22.387
We worked with Mr. Giuliani
because the President

00:05:22.387 --> 00:05:24.090
directed us to do so.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.457
-He literally said over and over

00:05:25.457 --> 00:05:27.092
"the President
told us to do this."

00:05:27.092 --> 00:05:29.695
And I believe it because no one
would work with Rudy Giuliani

00:05:29.695 --> 00:05:31.531
unless they were ordered to.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:34.233
Working with Rudy is like when
your mom makes you hang out

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:36.002
with her friend's weird son.

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:38.337
"Why don't you take Rudy
to the mall with you?"

00:05:38.337 --> 00:05:41.674
"Because he smells like onions
and he never stops screaming!"

00:05:41.674 --> 00:05:43.643
After Sondland made clear
he carried out

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:46.145
the President's orders, he went
on to explain specifically

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:49.047
that what Rudy Giuliani wanted
was definitely a quid pro quo,

00:05:49.047 --> 00:05:50.549
and that he did it specifically

00:05:50.549 --> 00:05:52.284
because that's what
Trump wanted.

00:05:52.284 --> 00:05:56.089
-Mr. Giuliani's request
were a quid pro quo

00:05:56.089 --> 00:06:00.760
for arranging a White House
visit for President Zelensky.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:05.564
Mr. Giuliani demanded that
Ukraine make a public statement

00:06:05.564 --> 00:06:07.867
announcing the investigations

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:14.106
of the 2016 election DNC server
and Burisma.

00:06:14.106 --> 00:06:17.309
Mr. Giuliani was
expressing the desires

00:06:17.309 --> 00:06:19.411
of the President
of the United States,

00:06:19.411 --> 00:06:23.849
and we knew these investigations
were important to the President.

00:06:23.849 --> 00:06:25.351
-There it is. He just said it.

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:28.120
This was a quid pro quo, and it
definitely makes sense to me

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:30.822
that Rudy was expressing
the desires of the President.

00:06:30.822 --> 00:06:33.759
Rudy looks like
the devil on Trump's shoulder

00:06:33.759 --> 00:06:35.761
except Trump would never
need a devil.

00:06:35.761 --> 00:06:37.329
"You should commit
quid pro quo."

00:06:37.329 --> 00:06:39.031
"Way ahead of you, tiny devil!"

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:40.899
[ Laughter ]

00:06:40.899 --> 00:06:44.370
Again Sondland made clear that
Trump had specifically directed

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.172
his administration,
people that actually work for

00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:48.874
the U.S. government and get paid
with your taxpayer dollars

00:06:48.874 --> 00:06:50.876
to orchestrate a quid pro quo
with Rudy Giuliani,

00:06:50.876 --> 00:06:52.845
who has no official
government role.

00:06:52.845 --> 00:06:55.281
And Sondland said
they were not happy about it.

00:06:55.281 --> 00:06:59.852
-President Trump directed us
to "talk with Rudy."

00:06:59.852 --> 00:07:02.554
We understood that
"talk with Rudy" meant

00:07:02.554 --> 00:07:08.460
talk with Mr. Rudy Giuliani,
the President's personal lawyer.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:10.796
Let me say again.

00:07:10.796 --> 00:07:13.132
We weren't happy with
the President's directive

00:07:13.132 --> 00:07:14.500
to "talk with Rudy."

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:15.834
-Of course they weren't happy.

00:07:15.834 --> 00:07:18.971
No one is happy to talk to Rudy.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:21.674
If you get cornered by Rudy
at a party, your only option

00:07:21.674 --> 00:07:23.776
is to pretend you're choking

00:07:23.776 --> 00:07:26.144
and even then Rudy would only
make things worse.

00:07:26.144 --> 00:07:28.414
"I know the Heimlich. Look!
I can do it on myself!"

00:07:28.414 --> 00:07:30.082
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:31.650
But this brings us
to a crucial point.

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:33.118
It wasn't just Trump and Rudy.

00:07:33.118 --> 00:07:35.154
Sondland made it clear that
a number of high-level officials

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:36.522
in the Trump White House

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:38.224
and some people outside
the White House were aware of

00:07:38.224 --> 00:07:39.825
what was happening
as it was happening.

00:07:39.825 --> 00:07:42.028
Sondland said he had e-mails
to support his account,

00:07:42.028 --> 00:07:45.364
and again, Sondland specifically
used the words "quid pro quo."

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:48.000
-These e-mails show that
the leadership

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:52.004
of the State Department,
the National Security Council,

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:53.505
and the White House

00:07:53.505 --> 00:07:56.942
were all informed about
the Ukraine efforts.

00:07:56.942 --> 00:08:00.179
I shared concerns of
the potential quid pro quo

00:08:00.179 --> 00:08:03.916
regarding the security aid
with Senator Ron Johnson.

00:08:03.916 --> 00:08:09.088
We kept the leadership of
the State Department and the NSC

00:08:09.088 --> 00:08:11.290
informed of our activities.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:16.395
And that included communications
with Secretary of State Pompeo.

00:08:16.395 --> 00:08:19.164
They knew what we were doing
and why.

00:08:19.164 --> 00:08:22.101
Everyone was in the loop.

00:08:22.101 --> 00:08:25.771
Again, everyone was in the loop.

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:28.607
-Think about that. He just said
everyone was in the loop,

00:08:28.607 --> 00:08:30.576
which makes clear once again
that these guys

00:08:30.576 --> 00:08:32.277
are the worst criminals
in the world.

00:08:32.277 --> 00:08:33.879
They orchestrated
an illicit scheme

00:08:33.879 --> 00:08:35.147
to pressure a foreign country

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:36.949
to interfere in
a presidential election,

00:08:36.949 --> 00:08:39.451
and they basically sent out
a staff-wide e-mail

00:08:39.451 --> 00:08:41.053
CCing everyone.

00:08:41.053 --> 00:08:43.489
Subject -- "Crimes."
"Hey, y'all, we're doing crimes.

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:45.758
Wanted to make sure
you all know about the crimes.

00:08:45.758 --> 00:08:47.593
If you have questions
about the crimes,

00:08:47.593 --> 00:08:51.263
please e-mail
crimes@whitehouse.gov/crimes."

00:08:51.263 --> 00:08:56.702
Sondland also said...
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:56.702 --> 00:09:00.039
...he also said he reviewed
other State Department documents

00:09:00.039 --> 00:09:01.941
that had been previously
not made public,

00:09:01.941 --> 00:09:04.910
which must have scared the hell
out of Giuliani and Trump.

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:07.546
-I've reviewed other
State Department documents,

00:09:07.546 --> 00:09:10.849
some of which are not currently
in the public domain,

00:09:10.849 --> 00:09:13.418
detailing
Mr. Giuliani's efforts.

00:09:13.418 --> 00:09:15.087
-The only part of that sentence
that shocks me

00:09:15.087 --> 00:09:16.588
is they weren't in
the public domain.

00:09:16.588 --> 00:09:19.291
Remember, Giuliani's already
done multiple TV interviews

00:09:19.291 --> 00:09:21.794
where he literally held up
his phone and his iPad

00:09:21.794 --> 00:09:23.896
to show off his communications
with Trump offi--

00:09:23.896 --> 00:09:26.532
I mean, I'm shocked Rudy didn't
come sprinting into the hearing

00:09:26.532 --> 00:09:28.801
with his phone in his hands,
screaming,

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:30.402
"He's right! I missed one!
It's right here!

00:09:30.402 --> 00:09:32.604
I got a selfie of me in Ukraine
with a shirt that says

00:09:32.604 --> 00:09:33.806
'I love quid pro quos!'"

00:09:33.806 --> 00:09:35.908
[ Laughter ]

00:09:35.908 --> 00:09:38.410
Sondland also provided
damning firsthand accounts

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:41.246
of his conversations with Trump
himself and had very specific

00:09:41.246 --> 00:09:43.950
recollections of phone calls
he had with the President

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:45.651
where he asked him
what was going on.

00:09:45.651 --> 00:09:49.121
-I thought it was a very bad
idea to hold that money.

00:09:49.121 --> 00:09:51.623
I finally called the President.

00:09:51.623 --> 00:09:52.992
I believe I just asked him

00:09:52.992 --> 00:09:55.026
an open-ended question,
Mr. Chairman.

00:09:55.026 --> 00:09:56.629
"What do you want from Ukraine?

00:09:56.629 --> 00:09:59.365
I keep hearing all these
different ideas and theories

00:09:59.365 --> 00:10:00.366
and this and that.

00:10:00.366 --> 00:10:01.800
What do you want?"

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:05.504
And it was a very short,
abrupt conversation.

00:10:05.504 --> 00:10:07.673
He was not in a good mood.

00:10:07.673 --> 00:10:10.141
-That doesn't surprise me.
Trump's never in a good mood.

00:10:10.141 --> 00:10:11.176
He only has two modes.

00:10:11.176 --> 00:10:12.778
He's either screaming
at reporters

00:10:12.778 --> 00:10:14.747
on the White House lawn
or glaring directly

00:10:14.747 --> 00:10:17.983
into the camera like a burglar
caught on a doorbell camera.

00:10:17.983 --> 00:10:19.317
I mean, look at him.

00:10:19.317 --> 00:10:22.087
Compare his face to the face
Nunes is always making.

00:10:22.087 --> 00:10:25.925
Nunes looks like a mailman
who just saw a Rottweiler

00:10:25.925 --> 00:10:27.460
and Trump is the Rottweiler.

00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:28.727
[ Laughter ]

00:10:28.727 --> 00:10:31.296
Now, Sondland had multiple
conversations with Trump.

00:10:31.296 --> 00:10:33.632
For example, you might remember
the infamous phone call

00:10:33.632 --> 00:10:36.902
Sondland had with Trump in which
Trump was overheard asking

00:10:36.902 --> 00:10:39.838
Sondland directly about
the investigations he wanted.

00:10:39.838 --> 00:10:42.774
A State Department official who
was with Sondland at the time

00:10:42.774 --> 00:10:45.211
also testified
that he overheard Sondland

00:10:45.211 --> 00:10:46.978
tell Trump that
the President of Ukraine

00:10:46.978 --> 00:10:50.516
would do anything for him
and that he "loves your ass."

00:10:50.516 --> 00:10:52.385
And again, Sondland confirmed

00:10:52.385 --> 00:10:54.586
that he did indeed
say that to Trump.

00:10:54.586 --> 00:10:58.791
-He also testified that
you confirmed to President Trump

00:10:58.791 --> 00:11:02.161
that you were in Ukraine
at the time

00:11:02.161 --> 00:11:05.897
and that President Zelensky
"loves your ass."

00:11:05.897 --> 00:11:07.966
Do you recall saying that?

00:11:07.966 --> 00:11:09.902
-Yeah, it sounds like something
I would say.

00:11:09.902 --> 00:11:12.270
[ Laughter ]

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:15.775
Putting it in Trump-speak
by saying he "loves your ass,

00:11:15.775 --> 00:11:17.509
he'll do whatever you want"

00:11:17.509 --> 00:11:20.178
meant that he would
really work with us.

00:11:20.178 --> 00:11:22.147
-And that's the President
we got.

00:11:22.147 --> 00:11:24.516
[ Laughter ]
I mean, the one who likes to

00:11:24.516 --> 00:11:28.186
know how foreign leaders feel at
any given moment about his ass.

00:11:28.186 --> 00:11:30.790
"Show them that picture of me
getting on the helicopter.

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.324
I think it looks really good
in that one."

00:11:32.324 --> 00:11:33.659
[ Laughter ]

00:11:33.659 --> 00:11:36.595
Now, today Trump responded to
Sondland's testimony

00:11:36.595 --> 00:11:37.763
on his way to Texas

00:11:37.763 --> 00:11:39.498
confirming that he spoke
to Sondland by phone.

00:11:39.498 --> 00:11:42.501
But at first his account of that
call made no sense whatsoever.

00:11:42.501 --> 00:11:46.504
-Just a quick comment on what's
going on in terms of testimony

00:11:46.504 --> 00:11:51.343
with Ambassador Sondland,
and I just noticed one thing,

00:11:51.343 --> 00:11:55.881
and I would say
that means it's all over.

00:11:55.881 --> 00:12:00.619
"What do you want from Ukraine?"
he asks me.

00:12:00.619 --> 00:12:04.456
Screaming, "What do you want
from Ukraine?

00:12:04.456 --> 00:12:07.926
I keep hearing all these
different ideas and theories."

00:12:07.926 --> 00:12:11.596
This is Ambassador Sondland
speaking to me.

00:12:11.596 --> 00:12:16.635
Just happened, to which
I turned off the television.

00:12:16.635 --> 00:12:18.137
"What do you want from Ukraine?

00:12:18.137 --> 00:12:21.273
I keep hearing all of these
different ideas and theories.

00:12:21.273 --> 00:12:24.243
What do you want?
What do you want?

00:12:24.243 --> 00:12:27.179
It was a very short
and abrupt conversation

00:12:27.179 --> 00:12:28.814
that he had with me.

00:12:28.814 --> 00:12:31.116
They said he was not
in a good mood."

00:12:31.116 --> 00:12:34.153
I'm always in a good mood.
I don't know what that is.

00:12:34.153 --> 00:12:37.122
-First of all, that's the worst
audition for a school play

00:12:37.122 --> 00:12:38.624
I've ever seen.
[ Laughter ]

00:12:38.624 --> 00:12:42.027
"Just so you know,
I'm not off book."

00:12:42.027 --> 00:12:43.562
Second, you're never
in a good mood.

00:12:43.562 --> 00:12:45.130
You're literally screaming
right now.

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:48.433
You can't scream,
"I'm always in a good mood."

00:12:48.433 --> 00:12:50.202
That's a sentence
that refutes itself.

00:12:50.202 --> 00:12:51.804
That's like a librarian
screaming,

00:12:51.804 --> 00:12:53.973
"Everyone keep your [bleep]
voices down!"

00:12:53.973 --> 00:12:55.273
[ Laughter ]

00:12:55.273 --> 00:12:57.075
Now, Trump went on to quote
Sondland's testimony.

00:12:57.075 --> 00:12:58.643
Sondland said that after months

00:12:58.643 --> 00:13:00.779
of following the President's
explicit orders to carry out

00:13:00.779 --> 00:13:02.414
the quid pro quo
he and Rudy wanted,

00:13:02.414 --> 00:13:03.982
he called Trump
to get a straight answer.

00:13:03.982 --> 00:13:07.519
Now, to be clear, this call
happened after the whistleblower

00:13:07.519 --> 00:13:10.422
wrote their report
and officials expressed concern

00:13:10.422 --> 00:13:11.490
about what Trump was doing.

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:13.191
So Trump suddenly
changed his tune

00:13:13.191 --> 00:13:14.894
and he told Sondland,
"Never mind.

00:13:14.894 --> 00:13:17.029
Forget about all of
that quid pro quo stuff."

00:13:17.029 --> 00:13:20.632
-It was a very short,
abrupt conversation.

00:13:20.632 --> 00:13:23.202
He was not in a good mood.

00:13:23.202 --> 00:13:25.237
And he just said,
"I want nothing. I want nothing.

00:13:25.237 --> 00:13:27.072
I want no quid pro quo.

00:13:27.072 --> 00:13:29.174
Tell Zelensky
to do the right thing,"

00:13:29.174 --> 00:13:30.743
something to that effect.

00:13:30.743 --> 00:13:32.645
This is the final word
that I heard from

00:13:32.645 --> 00:13:34.379
the President
of the United States.

00:13:34.379 --> 00:13:35.513
-So here's my answer.

00:13:35.513 --> 00:13:37.883
I want nothing. I want nothing.

00:13:37.883 --> 00:13:41.187
I want no quid pro quo.

00:13:41.187 --> 00:13:44.089
Tell Zelensky
to do the right thing.

00:13:44.089 --> 00:13:47.459
Then he says,
"This is the final word from

00:13:47.459 --> 00:13:49.961
the President
of the United States."

00:13:49.961 --> 00:13:51.330
-Yeah, but no, it's not.

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:52.664
You already got caught.

00:13:52.664 --> 00:13:54.666
That doesn't make you
sound innocent.

00:13:54.666 --> 00:13:56.768
That sounds like the way
a criminal talks

00:13:56.768 --> 00:13:59.037
when he thinks
his phone is tapped.

00:13:59.037 --> 00:14:01.807
"I want nothing,
certainly not a quid pro quo

00:14:01.807 --> 00:14:03.375
since that would be illegal.

00:14:03.375 --> 00:14:07.378
And now I'm off to church
because I'm a good boy."

00:14:07.378 --> 00:14:11.416
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:14:11.416 --> 00:14:13.218
But if you're looking for
one single image

00:14:13.218 --> 00:14:15.053
to capture everything
that happened today,

00:14:15.053 --> 00:14:16.255
I direct you to this photo of

00:14:16.255 --> 00:14:18.724
Sondland looking directly
into the camera

00:14:18.724 --> 00:14:20.359
during a break in the hearing.

00:14:20.359 --> 00:14:23.095
Damn, I mean,
he smelt it and dealt it.

00:14:23.095 --> 00:14:25.230
[ Laughter ]

00:14:25.230 --> 00:14:27.499
He looks like he's
in the opening credits

00:14:27.499 --> 00:14:29.068
of "The Real Housewives."

00:14:29.068 --> 00:14:30.469
[ Laughter ]

00:14:30.469 --> 00:14:32.237
"My name is Gordon.

00:14:32.237 --> 00:14:35.207
I may not quid or quo,
but I'm definitely a pro."

00:14:35.207 --> 00:14:36.608
[ Laughter ]

00:14:36.608 --> 00:14:39.044
Seriously, he looks like he just
threw a match on a building

00:14:39.044 --> 00:14:40.546
soaked in gasoline.

00:14:40.546 --> 00:14:41.813
[ Laughter ]

00:14:41.813 --> 00:14:43.648
Today was certainly
the most devastating day

00:14:43.648 --> 00:14:45.150
in the impeachment process
so far,

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:46.718
and perhaps
the most devastating day

00:14:46.718 --> 00:14:47.719
in the Trump presidency,

00:14:47.719 --> 00:14:49.454
a key witness to
the corrupt quid pro quo

00:14:49.454 --> 00:14:51.490
said he was following the orders
of the President

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:52.924
and named several
senior officials

00:14:52.924 --> 00:14:54.193
who also knew about the scheme

00:14:54.193 --> 00:14:56.528
and the Republican defense
crumbled before our eyes.

00:14:56.528 --> 00:14:57.596
This is it.

00:14:57.596 --> 00:14:58.998
If Republicans had any integrity
at all,

00:14:58.998 --> 00:15:01.066
they'd look at the evidence
and tell Trump...

00:15:01.066 --> 00:15:02.834
-That means it's all over.

00:15:02.834 --> 00:15:05.037
-This has been "A Closer Look."

